<node id="A.1">
  <data key="d0">A.1</data>
  <data key="d1">section</data>
  <data key="d2">Section A.1 provides detailed dataset statistics for the DocBench and MMLongBench multi-modal benchmarks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-76a69463e145e164e890b6c29aba9ec0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642292</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A.2">
  <data key="d0">A.2</data>
  <data key="d1">section</data>
  <data key="d2">Section A.2 showcases additional case studies that demonstrate RAG-Anything’s structure-aware capabilities across diverse multimodal content understanding tasks.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-76a69463e145e164e890b6c29aba9ec0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642292</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A.3">
  <data key="d0">A.3</data>
  <data key="d1">section</data>
  <data key="d2">Section A.3 documents the complete set of multimodal analysis prompts for vision, table, and equation processing that enable context-aware interpretation.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-76a69463e145e164e890b6c29aba9ec0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642292</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="A.4">
  <data key="d0">A.4</data>
  <data key="d1">section</data>
  <data key="d2">Section A.4 provides the standardized accuracy evaluation prompt used for consistent response assessment across all experimental conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-76a69463e145e164e890b6c29aba9ec0</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642292</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Graph-Enhanced Retrieval-Augmented Generation">
  <data key="d0">Graph-Enhanced Retrieval-Augmented Generation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Graph-Enhanced Retrieval-Augmented Generation addresses the limitations of large language models with long-context inputs and multi-hop queries by introducing explicit relational modeling.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de93d4b6f02e5ae737b9b9e8142401cd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642292</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GraphRAG">
  <data key="d0">GraphRAG</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">GraphRAG is a reference method for text-based knowledge graph construction.&lt;SEP&gt;GraphRAG is a specific implementation of Graph-Enhanced Retrieval-Augmented Generation, focusing on optimizing structures for retrieval efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de93d4b6f02e5ae737b9b9e8142401cd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642292</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="LightRAG">
  <data key="d0">LightRAG</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">LightRAG is a reference method for text-based knowledge graph construction, specifically designed as a graph-enhanced RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) system that integrates structured knowledge representation with dual-level retrieval mechanisms. It is also a sparsified index approach within the GraphRAG framework, optimized for retrieval efficiency. LightRAG has demonstrated moderate performance, achieving 85.0% accuracy in the 'Multimodal' document type and 59.7% in the 'Text-only' domain. The method shows the best accuracy in 'Research Reports/Introductions' and the worst in 'Guidebooks'. LightRAG is primarily a text-only content processing framework, used in various case studies to answer questions, including those about visual documents and financial table navigation. However, it has also been noted to provide incorrect answers in visual analysis tasks, with one instance of an AI model from LightRAG giving an incorrect response.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d4727f37ea1b30518f13dc89ffc7ea1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3199f24e41812cb62bea94f7c85f2636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfc6c28e224a59948d1c3f970cd333d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a411e34e853ae45bfd9bcee5b30fdc44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3030640e3aa96c21a21f63f845339bb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7b65a77beeebaa7ba6c82a6b282bc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-514397fe4b91c504d493b81ae4f2af0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc6b663130fa82a15ae0568ebdd7e714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e67b53472cda54f4238a2ccf98da3bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26f9e861c68e93709074930b8e53d41c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643535</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GNN-RAG">
  <data key="d0">GNN-RAG</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">GNN-RAG is a neural model variant within the GraphRAG framework, enhancing retrieval efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642292</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="HippoRAG">
  <data key="d0">HippoRAG</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">HippoRAG is a memory-augmented variant within the GraphRAG framework, improving retrieval efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642292</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RAPTOR">
  <data key="d0">RAPTOR</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">RAPTOR is a hierarchical method within the GraphRAG framework, integrating information for multi-level reasoning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642292</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ArchRAG">
  <data key="d0">ArchRAG</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">ArchRAG is a hierarchical method within the GraphRAG framework, integrating information for multi-level reasoning.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642292</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VideoRAG">
  <data key="d0">VideoRAG</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">VideoRAG is a dual-channel architecture for video understanding, employed in multimodal RAG systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642293</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MM-VID">
  <data key="d0">MM-VID</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MM-VID converts videos to text, addressing the need to integrate external knowledge from diverse data modalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642293</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="VisRAG">
  <data key="d0">VisRAG</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">VisRAG preserves document layouts as images, addressing the need to integrate external knowledge from diverse data modalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642293</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MMGraphRAG">
  <data key="d0">MMGraphRAG</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">MMGraphRAG is a multimodal retrieval framework that constructs unified knowledge graphs spanning textual and visual content, linking scene graphs with textual representations to integrate external knowledge from diverse data modalities. It has achieved 67.6% accuracy in the 'Multimodal' document type and 60.5% in the 'Text-only' domain, performing similarly to LightRAG. MMGraphRAG treats tables and equations as plain text and includes basic image processing. It is used in case studies to answer questions about visual documents, but has also been noted for providing incorrect answers in financial table navigation and visual analysis. MMGraphRAG is one of the RAG systems analyzed, outputting a text response to the question.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d4727f37ea1b30518f13dc89ffc7ea1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de93d4b6f02e5ae737b9b9e8142401cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3199f24e41812cb62bea94f7c85f2636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfc6c28e224a59948d1c3f970cd333d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a411e34e853ae45bfd9bcee5b30fdc44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3030640e3aa96c21a21f63f845339bb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7b65a77beeebaa7ba6c82a6b282bc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-514397fe4b91c504d493b81ae4f2af0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc6b663130fa82a15ae0568ebdd7e714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e67b53472cda54f4238a2ccf98da3bdd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643538</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal Retrieval-Augmented Generation">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Retrieval-Augmented Generation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multimodal Retrieval-Augmented Generation represents a natural evolution from text-based RAG systems, integrating external knowledge from diverse data modalities.&lt;SEP&gt;Multimodal Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) is a method used to evaluate the performance of systems in handling diverse and complex document types.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19c485068d1b3af6c308fbeb4976b40e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643543</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ask in any modality">
  <data key="d0">Ask in any modality</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Ask in any modality is a comprehensive survey on multimodal retrieval-augmented generation, highlighting the need for adaptive spatial reasoning and layout-aware parsing mechanisms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-f5f0a5a74b5a4eac43772c74649ca651</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642293</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
