<node id="Cross-Modal Knowledge Graph">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Modal Knowledge Graph</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Cross-Modal Knowledge Graph is a graph that integrates non-textual content with textual descriptions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cross-Modal Knowledge Graph is a knowledge graph constructed from non-textual modalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1025c419093621f01b9bd6bda58a4d8b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643551</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Text-Based Knowledge Graph">
  <data key="d0">Text-Based Knowledge Graph</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Text-Based Knowledge Graph is a traditional knowledge graph constructed from textual content.&lt;SEP&gt;The Text-Based Knowledge Graph is a knowledge graph constructed from textual information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1025c419093621f01b9bd6bda58a4d8b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643551</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal Knowledge Graph">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Knowledge Graph</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Multimodal Knowledge Graph is a graph that combines textual and non-textual content.&lt;SEP&gt;Multimodal Knowledge Graph is a graph that unifies knowledge across different modalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f0dae3e849332dc4c4fecee687039a4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643547</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal Entity Node">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Entity Node</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multimodal Entity Node is a node in the multimodal knowledge graph that represents non-textual content.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642297</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Intra-chunk Entities">
  <data key="d0">Intra-chunk Entities</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Intra-chunk Entities are entities identified within a single atomic content unit.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Relations">
  <data key="d0">Relations</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Relations are the connections between entities in the knowledge graph.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Entity Alignment">
  <data key="d0">Entity Alignment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Entity Alignment is the process of identifying semantically equivalent entities across different knowledge graphs.&lt;SEP&gt;Entity Alignment is a process of aligning entities across different modalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f0dae3e849332dc4c4fecee687039a4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Graph Fusion">
  <data key="d0">Graph Fusion</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Graph Fusion is the process of merging the cross-modal and text-based knowledge graphs.&lt;SEP&gt;Graph Fusion is a process of integrating graphs from different sources.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f0dae3e849332dc4c4fecee687039a4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dense Representation Generation">
  <data key="d0">Dense Representation Generation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dense Representation Generation is the process of creating unified embeddings for graph entities and relationships.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unified Knowledge Graph">
  <data key="d0">Unified Knowledge Graph</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Unified Knowledge Graph is the final graph that combines both multimodal and text-based knowledge.&lt;SEP&gt;Unified Knowledge Graph represents the combined structural knowledge and embedding table for efficient cross-modal retrieval.&lt;SEP&gt;Unified Knowledge Graph is a graph that includes entities, relationships, and atomic content chunks across different modalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ff6101b55afb188a8b2aba9f83cd92</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643557</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Embedding Table">
  <data key="d0">Embedding Table</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Embedding Table is a table that contains dense representations of graph entities, relationships, and atomic content chunks.&lt;SEP&gt;Embedding Table stores the dense vector representations of knowledge components for efficient retrieval.&lt;SEP&gt;Embedding Table is a critical component of the RAG-Anything framework, storing dense vector representations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ff6101b55afb188a8b2aba9f83cd92</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643557</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal Large Language Models">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Large Language Models</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Multimodal Large Language Models are used by RAG-Anything to derive textual representations from non-textual content.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-eac0008c777dab7291aec281277e77a1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642298</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GPT-4o-mini">
  <data key="d0">GPT-4o-mini</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">GPT-4o-mini is a powerful multimodal language model with native text and image understanding capabilities. It is used in various experimental frameworks and case studies, including accuracy evaluations and comprehensive experimental consistency and reliability checks. GPT-4o-mini achieved 61.0% overall accuracy on the DocBench Dataset, performing particularly well in 'Tutorials/Workshops' and poorly in 'Academic Papers'. In some case studies, it provided incorrect answers, such as in financial table navigation and visual analysis. Despite these limitations, GPT-4o-mini is a key model used for answering questions about visual documents and comparing responses in experimental evaluations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d4727f37ea1b30518f13dc89ffc7ea1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7aefd567d430c404aab77872282400eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfc6c28e224a59948d1c3f970cd333d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a411e34e853ae45bfd9bcee5b30fdc44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3030640e3aa96c21a21f63f845339bb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d68c9b009fe16eb1ecc9d4a748e081f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7b65a77beeebaa7ba6c82a6b282bc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-514397fe4b91c504d493b81ae4f2af0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc6b663130fa82a15ae0568ebdd7e714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e67b53472cda54f4238a2ccf98da3bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26f9e861c68e93709074930b8e53d41c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f162fe747d4504218a5bc094c97cc4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643546</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="DocBench">
  <data key="d0">DocBench</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">DocBench is a multimodal benchmark dataset used to evaluate the performance of RAG-Anything and other retrieval and augmentation methods. Specifically, DocBench consists of 229 documents, each averaging 66 pages and 46,377 tokens, across five critical domains, with financial reports being the most extensive category. These documents are used to assess model performance on both long and shorter documents, as well as for ablation studies in the context of document reasoning tasks. The benchmark spans a range of document types and includes 1,102 questions, making it a comprehensive tool for evaluating document understanding systems. DocBench is particularly useful for evaluating the performance of multimodal retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) systems, providing a robust framework for comparing different approaches in the field.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d4727f37ea1b30518f13dc89ffc7ea1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de93d4b6f02e5ae737b9b9e8142401cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3199f24e41812cb62bea94f7c85f2636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3030640e3aa96c21a21f63f845339bb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19c485068d1b3af6c308fbeb4976b40e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b7a22ef18d1df90b09c6752fdaa849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7b65a77beeebaa7ba6c82a6b282bc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c1dc026d368316a0e447d9d04cb5bc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc6b663130fa82a15ae0568ebdd7e714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55d457152e0dea0c28144e5e94403cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a534f8987f70ae30ffc6f998509f96a7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643542</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MMLongBench">
  <data key="d0">MMLongBench</data>
  <data key="d1">dataset</data>
  <data key="d2">MMLongBench is a multimodal benchmark dataset primarily used to evaluate the performance of models on long-context documents. It is designed to assess the effectiveness of methods in handling longer documents and is particularly relevant for long-document reasoning tasks. The dataset contains 135 documents, each averaging 47.5 pages and 21,214 tokens, across 7 document types, with 1,082 questions. These documents include a variety of types such as research reports, tutorials, and academic papers, which maintain moderate lengths. MMLongBench is utilized in multimodal document understanding tasks and is also relevant for validating the effectiveness of RAG-Anything, a specific multimodal benchmark.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d4727f37ea1b30518f13dc89ffc7ea1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de93d4b6f02e5ae737b9b9e8142401cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6489e2fb8e8849e9fba34fe5f95e4a0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3199f24e41812cb62bea94f7c85f2636&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfc6c28e224a59948d1c3f970cd333d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a411e34e853ae45bfd9bcee5b30fdc44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-841b2e1a62bf11ef382f155dc5fd836b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0b7a22ef18d1df90b09c6752fdaa849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc6b663130fa82a15ae0568ebdd7e714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55d457152e0dea0c28144e5e94403cb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a534f8987f70ae30ffc6f998509f96a7</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643527</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="MinerU">
  <data key="d0">MinerU</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">MinerU is a tool used to parse documents and extract text, images, tables, and equations for downstream RAG processing.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-2d4727f37ea1b30518f13dc89ffc7ea1</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
