<node id="Text-Centric Retrieval Bias">
  <data key="d0">Text-Centric Retrieval Bias</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Text-Centric Retrieval Bias is a failure pattern in multimodal RAG systems where they exhibit a strong preference for textual sources.&lt;SEP&gt;Text-Centric Retrieval Bias describes the tendency of systems to favor textual sources over visual information, even when visual data is relevant.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7aefd567d430c404aab77872282400eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26f9e861c68e93709074930b8e53d41c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Document Structure Processing Challenges">
  <data key="d0">Document Structure Processing Challenges</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Document Structure Processing Challenges is a failure pattern in multimodal RAG systems where they struggle with complex layouts and nonlinear information flows.&lt;SEP&gt;Document Structure Processing Challenges refer to difficulties in handling complex layouts and nonlinear information flows.&lt;SEP&gt;Document Structure Processing Challenges highlight the difficulties systems face with complex layouts and nonlinear information flows, exposing limitations in spatial reasoning and contextual understanding.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7aefd567d430c404aab77872282400eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e67b53472cda54f4238a2ccf98da3bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26f9e861c68e93709074930b8e53d41c</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643559</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Modal Misalignment">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Modal Misalignment</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cross-Modal Misalignment is a failure scenario where multimodal RAG systems consistently produce incorrect answers despite having access to necessary information.&lt;SEP&gt;Cross-Modal Misalignment is a failure scenario where systems produce incorrect answers despite having access to necessary information.&lt;SEP&gt;Cross-Modal Misalignment is a failure scenario where systems consistently produce incorrect answers despite having access to necessary information, indicating fundamental limitations in handling noisy, heterogeneous multimodal data.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-7aefd567d430c404aab77872282400eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e67b53472cda54f4238a2ccf98da3bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26f9e861c68e93709074930b8e53d41c</data>
