<node id="Multimodal Reality">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Reality</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multimodal Reality refers to the inherent heterogeneity and multimodality of real-world knowledge repositories.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal Knowledge Unification">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Knowledge Unification</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Multimodal Knowledge Unification is a process that decomposes raw inputs into atomic knowledge units while preserving their structural context and semantic alignment.&lt;SEP&gt;Multimodal Knowledge Unification is the process formalized by the equation, ensuring that the framework can handle and process various types of content in a consistent and structured manner.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-dded67fd8182de2201aa35ccbb4c8cd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abcce11b032cb7a3594b3a1302046124</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643549</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retrieval Index">
  <data key="d0">Retrieval Index</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Retrieval Index is the combination of Unified Knowledge Graph and Embedding Table used for efficient cross-modal retrieval.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RAG Methods">
  <data key="d0">RAG Methods</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">RAG Methods refer to traditional Retrieval-Augmented Generation methods that face limitations in handling multimodal documents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross-Modal Hybrid Retrieval Mechanism">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Modal Hybrid Retrieval Mechanism</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cross-Modal Hybrid Retrieval Mechanism is a framework introduced to address the limitations of traditional RAG methods by leveraging structural knowledge and semantic representations across heterogeneous modalities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Modality-Aware Query Encoding">
  <data key="d0">Modality-Aware Query Encoding</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Modality-Aware Query Encoding is a process that analyzes user queries to extract lexical cues and potential modality preferences.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unified Text Embedding">
  <data key="d0">Unified Text Embedding</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Unified Text Embedding is a unified text embedding computed using the same encoder as during indexing, ensuring consistency between query and knowledge representations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hybrid Knowledge Retrieval Architecture">
  <data key="d0">Hybrid Knowledge Retrieval Architecture</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Hybrid Knowledge Retrieval Architecture combines two complementary mechanisms: Structural Knowledge Navigation and Semantic Similarity Matching.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Structural Knowledge Navigation">
  <data key="d0">Structural Knowledge Navigation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Structural Knowledge Navigation addresses the challenge of capturing explicit relationships and multi-hop reasoning patterns by exploiting the structural properties of the Unified Knowledge Graph.&lt;SEP&gt;Structural Knowledge Navigation is a method for navigating the Knowledge Graph.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1025c419093621f01b9bd6bda58a4d8b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Semantic Similarity Matching">
  <data key="d0">Semantic Similarity Matching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Semantic Similarity Matching addresses the challenge of identifying semantically relevant knowledge that lacks explicit structural connections by conducting dense vector similarity search.&lt;SEP&gt;Semantic Similarity Matching is a method for matching queries to information in the Vector Database.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1025c419093621f01b9bd6bda58a4d8b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643552</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Candidate Pool Unification">
  <data key="d0">Candidate Pool Unification</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Candidate Pool Unification combines candidates from both retrieval pathways into a comprehensive candidate pool to ensure comprehensive coverage of relevant knowledge.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multi-Signal Fusion Scoring">
  <data key="d0">Multi-Signal Fusion Scoring</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Multi-Signal Fusion Scoring is a sophisticated fusion scoring mechanism that integrates multiple relevance signals to rank final candidates.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hybrid Retrieval Integration">
  <data key="d0">Hybrid Retrieval Integration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Hybrid Retrieval Integration leverages the complementary strengths of both knowledge graphs and dense representations for comprehensive coverage of relevant multimodal knowledge.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642303</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Textual Context">
  <data key="d0">Textual Context</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Textual Context is a structured textual context constructed from top-ranked retrieval candidates, including entity summaries, relationship descriptions, and chunk contents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Retrieval-Augmented Generation">
  <data key="d0">Retrieval-Augmented Generation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Retrieval-Augmented Generation methods are traditional approaches that face limitations in handling multimodal documents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ea106f7be2831088c0a1118ecb40eee8</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Visual Content">
  <data key="d0">Visual Content</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Visual content refers to images and diagrams that contain precise, structured data such as specific numerical values or detailed spatial relationships.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Text Content">
  <data key="d0">Text Content</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Text content typically provides general, conceptual descriptions and operates at a different granularity level than visual content.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Semantic Misalignment">
  <data key="d0">Semantic Misalignment</data>
  <data key="d1">category</data>
  <data key="d2">Semantic misalignment introduces noise that actively misleads the reasoning process due to the mismatch between visual and text content.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Top-to-Bottom and Left-to-Right Scanning Patterns">
  <data key="d0">Top-to-Bottom and Left-to-Right Scanning Patterns</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Current visual processing models default to sequential scanning patterns that mirror natural reading conventions.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sequential Scanning Patterns">
  <data key="d0">Sequential Scanning Patterns</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Sequential scanning patterns are a rigid spatial processing pattern that are effective for simple text documents but create systematic failures with structurally complex real-world content.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Non-Conventional Processing Strategies">
  <data key="d0">Non-Conventional Processing Strategies</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Non-conventional processing strategies are required for documents with complex structures such as tables, technical diagrams, and scientific figures.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Table">
  <data key="d0">Table</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Tables require column-wise interpretation and can embed critical information in unexpectedly positioned annotations.&lt;SEP&gt;Tables are a modality type that can be extracted from knowledge sources.&lt;SEP&gt;The table provides a detailed breakdown of document types and their associated statistics from the MMLongBench benchmark.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6489e2fb8e8849e9fba34fe5f95e4a0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1025c419093621f01b9bd6bda58a4d8b</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643527</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Technical Diagram">
  <data key="d0">Technical Diagram</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Technical diagrams follow specific directional flows and can contain critical information.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Scientific Figure">
  <data key="d0">Scientific Figure</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Scientific figures can contain critical information in unexpectedly positioned annotations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="GEM Row">
  <data key="d0">GEM Row</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The GEM row in the table lacks dedicated cell boundaries, leading to parsing ambiguities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642304</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Joint Column">
  <data key="d0">Joint Column</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The "Joint" column in the table merges with the "Slot" column without clear separation, creating parsing ambiguities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Slot Column">
  <data key="d0">Slot Column</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The "Slot" column in the table merges with the "Joint" column without clear separation, creating parsing ambiguities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="RAG Systems">
  <data key="d0">RAG Systems</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">RAG systems are currently brittle and require layout-aware parsing mechanisms to recognize and adapt to structural irregularities.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG Systems are multimodal retrieval-augmented generation systems evaluated using the DocBench benchmark.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19c485068d1b3af6c308fbeb4976b40e</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643543</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Layout-Aware Parsing Mechanisms">
  <data key="d0">Layout-Aware Parsing Mechanisms</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Layout-aware parsing mechanisms can recognize and adapt to structural irregularities in documents.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Visual Processing Capabilities">
  <data key="d0">Visual Processing Capabilities</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Visual processing capabilities can leverage spatial relationships and contextual design cues that are lost in purely structural representations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791642305</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Figure 12">
  <data key="d0">Figure 12</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure 12 is a visual representation used to illustrate the structural ambiguity in a table layout.&lt;SEP&gt;Figure 12 presents a failure scenario where all methods fail to correctly parse the confusing table layout with merged cells and unclear column boundaries.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-18ade91e917d2c67b94279ae6220dd06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e67b53472cda54f4238a2ccf98da3bdd</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
