<node id="RAG-Anything Framework">
  <data key="d0">RAG-Anything Framework</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">RAG-Anything Framework is a framework that addresses the challenges of multimodal knowledge representation and retrieval.&lt;SEP&gt;The RAG-Anything Framework is a specific implementation of the Universal RAG Framework.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG-Anything Framework is a framework used in the dual-graph construction phase to build a unified knowledge graph from multimodal content.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG-Anything Framework is a framework for constructing multimodal knowledge graphs.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG-Anything Framework is a framework that aims to build a unified knowledge representation across different modalities.&lt;SEP&gt;RAG-Anything Framework is a system designed to test long-context understanding and multimodal document comprehension.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9f0dae3e849332dc4c4fecee687039a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abcce11b032cb7a3594b3a1302046124&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1025c419093621f01b9bd6bda58a4d8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ff6101b55afb188a8b2aba9f83cd92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9db98ce0de085186d020ad648b70ae3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a534f8987f70ae30ffc6f998509f96a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c1dc026d368316a0e447d9d04cb5bc4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643547</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Graph Theory">
  <data key="d0">Graph Theory</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Graph Theory is a branch of mathematics that deals with the study of graphs and their properties.&lt;SEP&gt;Graph Theory is a branch of mathematics dealing with the study of graphs.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9f0dae3e849332dc4c4fecee687039a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abcce11b032cb7a3594b3a1302046124</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643547</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal Knowledge Graph Construction">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Knowledge Graph Construction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The process of constructing a Multimodal Knowledge Graph, which is a key component of the RAG-Anything framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-9f0dae3e849332dc4c4fecee687039a4</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Equation">
  <data key="d0">Equation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Equations are a modality type that can be extracted from knowledge sources.&lt;SEP&gt;(\(\mathcal{V}_j, \mathcal{E}_j\) = R(\(d_j^{chunk}\))) is a key component in the RAG-Anything framework, defining the process of generating a structured graph representation from a chunk of multimodal content.&lt;SEP&gt;The equation \(\mathcal{T} = \mathrm{emb}(s) : s \in \mathcal{V} \cup \mathcal{E} \cup c_{j_j}\) is a key component in the RAG-Anything framework.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abcce11b032cb7a3594b3a1302046124&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1025c419093621f01b9bd6bda58a4d8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ff6101b55afb188a8b2aba9f83cd92</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dual-Graph Construction Phase">
  <data key="d0">Dual-Graph Construction Phase</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dual-Graph Construction Phase is a phase in the RAG-Anything framework where the equation \((\mathcal{V}_j, \mathcal{E}_j) = R(d_j^{chunk})\) is used to construct a graph from a chunk of multimodal content.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abcce11b032cb7a3594b3a1302046124</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chunk Decomposition">
  <data key="d0">Chunk Decomposition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Chunk Decomposition is a process where the function \(R\) decomposes the chunk of content into its constituent parts, such as text, images, tables, and equations.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abcce11b032cb7a3594b3a1302046124</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Entity Extraction">
  <data key="d0">Entity Extraction</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Entity Extraction is a process where the function \(R\) identifies entities and their attributes, such as names, types, and descriptions, from the decomposed content.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abcce11b032cb7a3594b3a1302046124</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Relationship Identification">
  <data key="d0">Relationship Identification</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Relationship Identification is a process where the function \(R\) identifies relationships between the extracted entities, forming the edges of the graph.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abcce11b032cb7a3594b3a1302046124</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Multimodal Content">
  <data key="d0">Multimodal Content</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Multimodal Content refers to a chunk of content that could be a figure, table, equation, or text segment.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abcce11b032cb7a3594b3a1302046124</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vertices">
  <data key="d0">Vertices</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Vertices (\(\mathcal{V}_j\)) represent the entities identified within the chunk.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abcce11b032cb7a3594b3a1302046124</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643549</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Edges">
  <data key="d0">Edges</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Edges (\(\mathcal{E}_j\)) represent the relationships between the entities.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-abcce11b032cb7a3594b3a1302046124</data>
  <data key="d4">/Users/drw/PycharmProjects/rag-anything-reproduction/data/RAG-Anything_arXiv_2025.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1791643549</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Function R">
